{
    "background_story": "Peter was a blacksmith's apprentice in a small medieval village. He spent most of his days hammering away at glowing ingots of metal, shaping them into tools and horseshoes. But Peter's true passion lay in crafting beautiful works of art from the molten metal. In his spare time, he would sneak into the forge and experiment with different techniques, creating intricate designs and patterns. One day, the village lord commissioned a grand suit of armor, and Peter saw his chance. He worked tirelessly, folding and shaping the ingots into a masterpiece of craftsmanship. The finished armor was a marvel, and Peter's skill was recognized throughout the land. He became known as the greatest armor-maker of his time, and his ingots were always in high demand.",
